1-33/08-2027/0768(A)-(S), valid to 26 August 2027.\nThe car park is served by a dedicated express ramp, and EV charging stations are provided.\n\nHow many units are there and how are the two towers arranged?\n\nM Aspira holds 1,618 serviced apartments in two towers over a shared podium — 686 units in Tower A and 932 in Tower B. Counted off the brochure's key plan, Tower A has 13 units to a floor and Tower B has 17. Tower B is set out in a single run so its front units look towards the KL city view, Tower A is arranged around the lift core with its outlook over the facilities deck, and a Sky Lounge sits at the top of Tower B.\n\nIs M Aspira freehold or leasehold?\n\nLeasehold. The lease runs 99 years and expires on 13 August 2123. The approving authority for the development is DBKL.\n\nCan foreigners buy at M Aspira?\n\nNo. M Aspira is not open to foreign purchase.\n\nWhen will M Aspira be completed?\n\nThe expected completion date is June 2029. That is the date printed in the statutory fine print on the back page of the developer's e-pamphlet.\n\nWho is the developer of M Aspira?\n\nMah Sing Properties Sdn Bhd, company number 199301010242. It holds developer licence 5911/09-2027/1524(A), valid to 26 September 2027, and advertising permit 5911-33/08-2027/0768(A)-(S), valid to 26 August 2027.\n\nWhat facilities does M Aspira have?\n\nLevel 13 carries twenty-one facilities: a 50 m lap pool, a children's pool and water play area, a jacuzzi, a sun deck and family deck, a gymnasium, indoor badminton and pickleball courts, a playground, a floating pavilion, a multi-purpose hall, a co-working space, a gourmet kitchen, outdoor dining and BBQ, a games room and children's play room, a glamping area and a hanging viewing deck. Level 1 holds retail lots, a nursery and kindergarten, a management office and a surau. The development is GreenRE certified and comes with EV charging stations, delivery parcel lockers and an automated waste collection system.\n\nFigures checked against 